// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 50 — Processes spawned at login
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Each line runs once when Niri starts. For daemons that support it,
// xdg-desktop-autostart (systemd) is an alternative.
//
// Tip: use spawn-sh-at-startup for shell pipelines or variable expansion.
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// Export XDG_MENU_PREFIX into the systemd user session and rebuild the
// sycoca database so KDE/Qt apps see the correct .desktop entries.
spawn-at-startup "bash" "-c" "systemctl --user import-environment XDG_MENU_PREFIX && kbuildsycoca6"

// Clipboard history: wl-paste watches the clipboard and cliphist stores it.
// Access via iNiR's clipboard overlay (Mod+V).
//
// The image's own /usr/share/niri/global.kdl — included first by config.kdl —
// already starts that watcher: `wl-paste --watch cliphist store`, with no
// `--type`, so it takes whatever the source offers, text or image. That is the
// watcher this session runs on, and the one iNiR's overlay reads.
//
// The image watcher below stays on, because it is the one that keeps iNiR's own
// window-preview frames out of the history: it checks the marker the compositor
// drops while it captures a preview and swallows that frame instead of storing
// it. It stores the same bytes the image's watcher does, and cliphist looks back
// through its last 100 entries for a duplicate, so that copy stays one entry.
//
// The text watcher is off. It is the same store with `--type text` piped
// through clipboard-store.py, which strips the markup when a copy offers only
// text/html — rich text out of Discord, Slack, VS Code, or a page editor like
// ChatGPT's. Running it beside the image's watcher is what put a copy in the
// history twice: the two payloads differ, so cliphist cannot collapse them, and
// the entry showed up once with its `<meta http-equiv=...>` header and once
// without. With it commented out every copy lands once, raw. Uncomment it if
// that stripping is worth the duplicate.
//
// RakuOS: the scripts ship with the package under /usr/share/quickshell/inir,
// not in a user copy of the payload, so these paths are absolute.
// spawn-at-startup "bash" "-c" "wl-paste --no-newline --type text --watch /usr/share/quickshell/inir/scripts/clipboard-store.py &"
spawn-at-startup "bash" "-c" "wl-paste --type image --watch /usr/share/quickshell/inir/scripts/clipboard-image-store.sh &"

// Polkit: the iNiR shell is the authentication agent (its dialogs follow the
// family you use). Spawning another agent here would take its place.

// ── iNiR shell ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// iNiR is managed by the user systemd service (inir.service).
// Do not add a compositor startup entry here or you'll get two shells.
